/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Chronicles chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2chronicles", [
{n:1, name:"Solomon Asks for Wisdom", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 1:7",verse:"In that night did God appear unto Solomon, and said unto him, Ask what I shall give thee."}, facts:["Did you know that Solomon offered one thousand burnt offerings in a single visit to Gibeon before God appeared to him that night? It was one of the largest sacrifices recorded in Scripture.","Did you know that in Solomon's day the tabernacle Moses made still stood at Gibeon while the ark rested in a tent in Jerusalem? The two had been separated since David brought the ark up to the capital.","Did you know that God opened His conversation with Solomon at Gibeon with a blank check: Ask what I shall give thee? Solomon asked for wisdom, and God added riches, wealth, and honour besides."], questions:[
{q:"Where did Solomon and all the congregation with him go to seek the LORD at the start of his reign?", options:["Gibeon","Jerusalem","Hebron","Bethel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:3",verse:"So Solomon, and all the congregation with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon; for there was the tabernacle of the congregation of God, which Moses the servant of the LORD had made in the wilderness.", insight:"Solomon began his reign by going where God was worshiped, not by tightening his grip on power. Starting with worship is still the wisest first move any leader can make."},
{q:"What stood at the high place in Gibeon?", options:["The tabernacle of the congregation, which Moses had made in the wilderness","The ark of the covenant","The temple Solomon would later build","The altar David built on Ornan's threshingfloor"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:3",verse:"So Solomon, and all the congregation with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon; for there was the tabernacle of the congregation of God, which Moses the servant of the LORD had made in the wilderness.", insight:"The old tabernacle still stood at Gibeon, a reminder that God keeps meeting His people across generations. What He honored in Moses' day, He still honored in Solomon's."},
{q:"Where was the ark of God at this time?", options:["In the tent David had pitched for it in Jerusalem","In the tabernacle at Gibeon","In the most holy place of the temple","Hidden beneath Mount Moriah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:4",verse:"But the ark of God had David brought up from Kirjath-jearim to the place which David had prepared for it: for he had pitched a tent for it at Jerusalem.", insight:"The ark and the tabernacle were miles apart, yet Solomon honored both. Faithfulness sometimes means holding together what history has scattered."},
{q:"Who had made the brasen altar that stood before the tabernacle at Gibeon?", options:["Bezaleel the son of Uri","Aholiab the son of Ahisamach","Huram the craftsman from Tyre","Solomon's overseers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:5",verse:"Moreover the brasen altar, that Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, had made, he put before the tabernacle of the LORD: and Solomon and the congregation sought unto it.", insight:"Bezaleel's altar had outlasted its maker by centuries. Work done for God with skill and care keeps serving long after our hands are gone."},
{q:"How many burnt offerings did Solomon offer on the brasen altar at Gibeon?", options:["A thousand","A hundred","Seven","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:6",verse:"And Solomon went up thither to the brasen altar before the LORD, which was at the tabernacle of the congregation, and offered a thousand burnt offerings upon it.", insight:"Solomon's generosity in worship was staggering, and God noticed. Lavish worship is never wasted; heaven always answers a whole heart."},
{q:"How many burnt offerings had Solomon offered at Gibeon before God appeared to him that night?", options:["A thousand","A hundred","Seven","Ten"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:6",verse:"And Solomon went up thither to the brasen altar before the LORD, which was at the tabernacle of the congregation, and offered a thousand burnt offerings upon it.", insight:"A thousand offerings went up before God spoke a word. Generous worship prepared the way for a generous answer."},
{q:"What did God say to Solomon when He appeared to him?", options:["Ask what I shall give thee.","Behold, I have given thee a wise and understanding heart.","Walk before me as David thy father walked.","I have heard thy prayer at Gibeon."], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:7",verse:"In that night did God appear unto Solomon, and said unto him, Ask what I shall give thee.", insight:"God opened with a blank check before Solomon asked for anything. God delights to invite us to ask, and His generosity runs ahead of our requests."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask God to give him?", options:["Wisdom and knowledge, to judge the people","Riches and long life","Victory over his enemies","A son to sit on his throne"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:10",verse:"Give me now wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people: for who can judge this thy people, that is so great?", insight:"Solomon asked for tools to serve others, not treasures for himself. The prayer that pleases God most is the one that aims at blessing people."},
{q:"To what did Solomon liken the multitude of the people he was made king over?", options:["The dust of the earth","The stars of heaven","The sand of the sea","The grass of the field"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:9",verse:"Now, O LORD God, let thy promise unto David my father be established: for thou hast made me king over a people like the dust of the earth in multitude.", insight:"Solomon felt the weight of ruling a people beyond counting. Feeling small before a big calling is not weakness; it is the beginning of wisdom."},
{q:"For whose sake did Solomon say God had shown great mercy in making him king?", options:["David his father","Abraham his forefather","Moses the servant of God","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:8",verse:"And Solomon said unto God, Thou hast shewed great mercy unto David my father, and hast made me to reign in his stead.", insight:"Solomon knew his throne was an inheritance of mercy, not a personal achievement. Remembering who opened the door keeps us humble inside the room."},
{q:"Why did Solomon say he needed wisdom and knowledge?", options:["To go out and come in before this great people, and to judge them","To build the temple with understanding","To answer the hard questions of the queen of Sheba","To write proverbs for his son"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:10",verse:"Give me now wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people: for who can judge this thy people, that is so great?", insight:"Solomon tied his request to his responsibility. Asking God for help is strongest when we can name exactly what the work requires."},
{q:"Besides wisdom and knowledge, what three things did God promise Solomon?", options:["Riches, wealth, and honour","Long life, peace, and sons","Victory, fame, and health","Silver, gold, and cattle"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:12",verse:"Wisdom and knowledge is granted unto thee; and I will give thee riches, and wealth, and honour, such as none of the kings have had that have been before thee, neither shall there any after thee have the like.", insight:"God added what Solomon never asked for. When we seek first what matters to God, He often entrusts us with more than we dared to request."},
{q:"What did God say about Solomon's riches and honour compared with other kings?", options:["No king before him or after him would have the like","Only David his father had received as much","They would last only while he obeyed","They would be divided among his twelve officers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:12",verse:"Wisdom and knowledge is granted unto thee; and I will give thee riches, and wealth, and honour, such as none of the kings have had that have been before thee, neither shall there any after thee have the like.", insight:"God's bonus to Solomon was unmatched in history. Faithfulness in the one ask opened the door to blessing beyond measure."},
{q:"How many chariots did Solomon gather?", options:["1,400","140","14,000","400"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:14",verse:"And Solomon gathered chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, which he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.", insight:"Solomon's kingdom grew strong and organized after Gibeon. Blessing from God often shows up as practical strength for the work ahead."},
{q:"How many horsemen did Solomon have?", options:["12,000","1,200","120,000","2,000"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:14",verse:"And Solomon gathered chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, which he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.", insight:"Twelve thousand horsemen speak of a kingdom at peace and in order. God can give both the wisdom to rule and the resources to secure what wisdom builds."},
{q:"Where did Solomon go after his night at Gibeon?", options:["Back to Jerusalem, to reign over Israel","To Egypt to buy horses","To Tyre to meet Huram","To Hebron to be anointed again"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:13",verse:"Then Solomon came from his journey to the high place that was at Gibeon to Jerusalem, from before the tabernacle of the congregation, and reigned over Israel.", insight:"After the vision comes the work; Solomon returned to Jerusalem to rule. Encounters with God are meant to send us back to our assignment, not away from it."},
{q:"What did the king make as plenteous in Jerusalem as stones?", options:["Silver and gold","Wheat and barley","Horses and chariots","Cedar and fir trees"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:15",verse:"And the king made silver and gold at Jerusalem as plenteous as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that are in the vale for abundance.", insight:"Under Solomon, precious metals became common as rocks. Prosperity follows wisdom, but the chapter is careful to show which came first."},
{q:"What trees did Solomon make to be as the sycamore trees in the vale?", options:["Cedars","Fir trees","Algum trees","Olive trees"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:15",verse:"And the king made silver and gold at Jerusalem as plenteous as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that are in the vale for abundance.", insight:"Even Lebanon's prized cedars became plentiful in Solomon's day. When God blesses, He does not do it halfway."},
{q:"From where did Solomon obtain horses?", options:["Egypt","Tyre","Arabia","Kedar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:16",verse:"And Solomon had horses brought out of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king’s merchants received the linen yarn at a price.", insight:"Solomon's merchants traded with Egypt for horses and linen yarn. Wisdom includes knowing how to build honest trade that strengthens the nation."},
{q:"What was the price of a chariot brought up out of Egypt?", options:["Six hundred shekels of silver","One hundred and fifty shekels of silver","Thirty shekels of silver","Fifty shekels of gold"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 1:17",verse:"And they fetched up, and brought forth out of Egypt a chariot for six hundred shekels of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so brought they out horses for all the kings of the Hittites, and for the kings of Syria, by their means.", insight:"Scripture even records the price: six hundred shekels for a chariot, one hundred fifty for a horse. God cares about the details of honest business, right down to the receipt."}
]},
{n:2, name:"Preparing to Build", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 2:5",verse:"And the house which I build is great: for great is our God above all gods."}, facts:["Did you know Solomon's building workforce numbered over 150,000 men: 70,000 burden bearers, 80,000 stonecutters, and 3,600 overseers? It was one of the largest construction projects of the ancient world.","Did you know the master craftsman Huram sent was of mixed heritage, the son of a Danite woman and a Tyrian father? His skill in gold, silver, bronze, and engraving fitted him for the finest work of the temple.","Did you know Solomon paid for the timber in food rather than gold: 20,000 measures each of wheat and barley, and 20,000 baths each of wine and oil, for Huram's servants?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Solomon determine to build?", options:["An house for the name of the LORD, and an house for his kingdom","A palace for Pharaoh's daughter and a house for the ark","Two temples, one at Gibeon and one at Jerusalem","A wall around Jerusalem and a tower in Lebanon"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:1",verse:"And Solomon determined to build an house for the name of the LORD, and an house for his kingdom.", insight:"Solomon planned God's house before his own, and named them in that order. What we put first in our plans reveals what we put first in our hearts."},
{q:"How many men did Solomon appoint to bear burdens?", options:["70,000","7,000","80,000","36,000"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:2",verse:"And Solomon told out threescore and ten thousand men to bear burdens, and fourscore thousand to hew in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred to oversee them.", insight:"Seventy thousand burden bearers, eighty thousand hewers, thirty-six hundred overseers: Solomon counted every role. Great visions need more than inspiration; they need careful organization and willing hands."},
{q:"In what order does the chapter list Solomon's three groups of workmen?", options:["70,000 to bear burdens, 80,000 to hew in the mountain, 3,600 overseers","80,000 to bear burdens, 70,000 to hew in the mountain, 3,600 overseers","70,000 to hew in the mountain, 80,000 to bear burdens, 3,600 overseers","3,600 overseers, 70,000 to bear burdens, 80,000 to hew in the mountain"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:2",verse:"And Solomon told out threescore and ten thousand men to bear burdens, and fourscore thousand to hew in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred to oversee them.", insight:"Solomon listed every group in order: burden bearers, hewers, overseers. God is a God of order, and every role in His work matters enough to be counted."},
{q:"How many overseers did Solomon set over the workmen?", options:["3,600","360","36,000","550"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:18",verse:"And he set threescore and ten thousand of them to be bearers of burdens, and fourscore thousand to be hewers in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred overseers to set the people a work.", insight:"Thirty-six hundred overseers kept the great workforce in order. Even holy work needs supervision; structure is how big callings stay honest."},
{q:"To which king did Solomon send his request for timber and a craftsman?", options:["Huram king of Tyre","The king of Sidon","Pharaoh king of Egypt","Benhadad king of Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:3",verse:"And Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, As thou didst deal with David my father, and didst send him cedars to build him an house to dwell therein, even so deal with me.", insight:"Solomon reached across borders for help, building on David's friendship with Huram. God often provides for His work through unexpected partners and old friendships."},
{q:"What had Huram previously sent to David?", options:["Cedars to build him an house","Gold and silver for the treasury","Ships for a navy at Eziongeber","Horses and chariots for his army"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:3",verse:"And Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, As thou didst deal with David my father, and didst send him cedars to build him an house to dwell therein, even so deal with me.", insight:"Huram had helped David, and now he would help David's son. Faithfulness in one generation opens doors for the next."},
{q:"Which three kinds of timber did Solomon ask Huram to send from Lebanon?", options:["Cedar trees, fir trees, and algum trees","Cedar, olive, and cypress","Fir, pine, and shittim wood","Cedar, algum, and sycamore"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:8",verse:"Send me also cedar trees, fir trees, and algum trees, out of Lebanon: for I know that thy servants can skill to cut timber in Lebanon; and, behold, my servants shall be with thy servants,", insight:"Solomon wanted the finest timber in the known world for God's house. Excellence in materials was his way of honoring the God the house was for."},
{q:"Why did Solomon say he needed so much timber?", options:["Because the house he would build would be great and wonderful","Because he was also building his own palace","Because the timber would be sold to other nations","Because the forests of Lebanon were being cleared"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:9",verse:"Even to prepare me timber in abundance: for the house which I am about to build shall be wonderful great.", insight:"The scale of the supply matched the scale of the vision. Big callings from God deserve big-hearted preparation."},
{q:"What kind of workman did Solomon ask Huram to send him?", options:["A man cunning to work in gold, silver, brass, iron, purple, crimson, and blue, who could grave","A master shipbuilder for a navy","A scribe to record the chronicles","A captain to train his horsemen"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:7",verse:"Send me now therefore a man cunning to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass, and in iron, and in purple, and crimson, and blue, and that can skill to grave with the cunning men that are with me in Judah and in Jerusalem, whom David my father did provide.", insight:"Solomon valued skilled craftsmen as much as raw materials. God honors the work of skilled hands, and wise leaders recruit the best for His service."},
{q:"With whose skilled men would Huram's craftsman work?", options:["The cunning men of David and of Solomon","The priests and the Levites","The elders of Israel","The servants of Pharaoh"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:7",verse:"Send me now therefore a man cunning to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass, and in iron, and in purple, and crimson, and blue, and that can skill to grave with the cunning men that are with me in Judah and in Jerusalem, whom David my father did provide.", insight:"Tyrian skill would labor side by side with Israelite skill. God's work is richer when different gifts and peoples build together."},
{q:"Why did Solomon say the house he built must be great?", options:["Because great is our God above all gods","Because all nations would come to see it","Because David had commanded it","Because the ark required a large room"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:5",verse:"And the house which I build is great: for great is our God above all gods.", insight:"This is the beating heart of the chapter: the building is great because God is great. Our efforts for God should always be sized to who He is, not to who we are."},
{q:"What did Solomon say about heaven's ability to contain God?", options:["The heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain him","The highest heaven can barely hold His glory","The temple would contain His fullness","The ark alone could contain His presence"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:6",verse:"But who is able to build him an house, seeing the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain him? who am I then, that I should build him an house, save only to burn sacrifice before him?", insight:"Even while building God's house, Solomon confessed no house could hold Him. True worship holds reverence and nearness together: God is close, yet never small."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask about himself in light of God's greatness?", options:["Who am I, that I should build him an house?","Am I not the son of David the king?","Have I not wealth enough for this?","Shall I find favour in His sight?"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:6",verse:"But who is able to build him an house, seeing the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain him? who am I then, that I should build him an house, save only to burn sacrifice before him?", insight:"The wisest king felt unworthy of the task, and said so. Humility does not shrink from God's work; it simply knows who deserves the credit."},
{q:"How many measures of beaten wheat did Solomon promise Huram's servants?", options:["20,000","2,000","10,000","100,000"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:10",verse:"And, behold, I will give to thy servants, the hewers that cut timber, twenty thousand measures of beaten wheat, and twenty thousand measures of barley, and twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.", insight:"Solomon paid generously in wheat, barley, wine, and oil. Those who labor for God's house deserve honest, generous wages."},
{q:"How many baths each of wine and oil were promised to Huram's servants?", options:["20,000","10,000","2,000","5,000"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:10",verse:"And, behold, I will give to thy servants, the hewers that cut timber, twenty thousand measures of beaten wheat, and twenty thousand measures of barley, and twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.", insight:"The provisions were measured out in abundance, twenty thousand baths each. God is not stingy with those who serve His purposes, and neither should we be."},
{q:"How did Huram answer Solomon's request?", options:["In writing","By sending messengers only","In person at Jerusalem","Through the elders of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:11",verse:"Then Huram the king of Tyre answered in writing, which he sent to Solomon, Because the LORD hath loved his people, he hath made thee king over them.", insight:"Huram's written reply became part of the record. Putting commitments in writing protects friendships and keeps everyone honest."},
{q:"Why did Huram say the LORD had made Solomon king over Israel?", options:["Because the LORD hath loved his people","Because David had defeated the Philistines","Because Solomon had paid him tribute","Because the lot had fallen to Solomon"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:11",verse:"Then Huram the king of Tyre answered in writing, which he sent to Solomon, Because the LORD hath loved his people, he hath made thee king over them.", insight:"Even a Gentile king saw that Solomon's throne was an act of God's love for Israel. God's goodness to His people is visible even to outsiders."},
{q:"Of which tribe was the mother of Huram's master craftsman?", options:["Dan","Judah","Levi","Naphtali"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:14",verse:"The son of a woman of the daughters of Dan, and his father was a man of Tyre, skilful to work in gold, and in silver, in brass, in iron, in stone, and in timber, in purple, in blue, and in fine linen, and in crimson; also to grave any manner of graving, and to find out every device which shall be put to him, with thy cunning men, and with the cunning men of my lord David thy father.", insight:"The craftsman's mother was a daughter of Dan and his father a Tyrian. God wove two peoples into one family to build His house, a quiet picture of His wider welcome."},
{q:"To which seaport would Huram's men bring the timber in floats by sea?", options:["Joppa","Tyre","Sidon","Gaza"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:16",verse:"And we will cut wood out of Lebanon, as much as thou shalt need: and we will bring it to thee in flotes by sea to Joppa; and thou shall carry it up to Jerusalem.", insight:"Logs cut in Lebanon would ride the sea to Joppa, then climb to Jerusalem. God moves provision through long, practical chains of ordinary work."},
{q:"How many strangers did Solomon number in the land of Israel?", options:["153,600","150,000","70,000","36,000"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 2:17",verse:"And Solomon numbered all the strangers that were in the land of Israel, after the numbering wherewith David his father had numbered them; and they were found an hundred and fifty thousand and three thousand and six hundred.", insight:"Solomon counted the resident aliens and gave them honorable work. In God's economy, the stranger is not a problem to manage but a worker to dignify."}
]},
{n:3, name:"The Temple Rises", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 3:1",verse:"Then Solomon began to build the house of the LORD at Jerusalem in mount Moriah, where the LORD appeared unto David his father, in the place that David had prepared in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite."}, facts:["Did you know the temple was built on Mount Moriah, the same mountain where Abraham was told to offer up Isaac? Solomon's temple stood on ground already sacred with the story of faith.","Did you know the two bronze pillars at the temple porch had personal names, Jachin on the right hand and Boaz on the left? Jachin means he shall establish, and Boaz means in him is strength.","Did you know the most holy place was overlaid with six hundred talents of fine gold, and even its nails weighed fifty shekels of gold apiece?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did Solomon begin to build the house of the LORD?", options:["In Jerusalem, in Mount Moriah","On Mount Gerizim near Shechem","At Gibeon on the high place","On Mount Carmel by the sea"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:1",verse:"Then Solomon began to build the house of the LORD at Jerusalem in mount Moriah, where the LORD appeared unto David his father, in the place that David had prepared in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite.", insight:"The temple rose on Mount Moriah, the very mountain of Abraham's sacrifice. God builds His greatest works on ground already marked by faith."},
{q:"When did Solomon begin to build the house of the LORD?", options:["In the second month of the fourth year of his reign","In the seventh month of his first year","In the first month of his tenth year","In the twelfth month of his seventh year"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:2",verse:"And he began to build in the second day of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign.", insight:"The second month of the fourth year: God's great works begin on God's timetable, and Scripture marks the date."},
{q:"When did Solomon begin to build the house?", options:["In the second month of the fourth year of his reign","In the seventh month of the first year","In the twelfth year, at the feast","In the fortieth year of David"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:2",verse:"And he began to build in the second day of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign.", insight:"Scripture dates the beginning precisely: second month, fourth year. God keeps a calendar for His promises, and His timing is worth noting."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the temple's foundation?", options:["Sixty cubits long and twenty cubits broad","Twenty cubits long and twenty broad","One hundred and twenty cubits long and twenty broad","Thirty-five cubits long and five broad"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:3",verse:"Now these are the things wherein Solomon was instructed for the building of the house of God. The length by cubits after the first measure was threescore cubits, and the breadth twenty cubits.", insight:"The house was sixty by twenty cubits, the same proportions as the tabernacle, doubled. God loves both continuity with the past and growth beyond it."},
{q:"How large was the porch that was in the front of the house?", options:["Twenty cubits long and a hundred and twenty high","Twenty cubits long and twenty high","Ten cubits long and thirty high","Thirty-five cubits long and five high"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:4",verse:"And the porch that was in the front of the house, the length of it was according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the height was an hundred and twenty: and he overlaid it within with pure gold.", insight:"The porch towered a hundred and twenty cubits, drawing every eye upward. Architecture can preach: some buildings are meant to lift the heart toward heaven."},
{q:"With what wood was the greater house ceiled?", options:["Fir tree","Cedar","Algum","Shittim wood"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:5",verse:"And the greater house he cieled with fir tree, which he overlaid with fine gold, and set thereon palm trees and chains.", insight:"Fir beams, overlaid with fine gold and carved with palms and chains. Even the ceiling, which few would study closely, was finished with care. God deserves our best in the unseen places too."},
{q:"What decorations were wrought on the gold overlay of the greater house?", options:["Palm trees and chains","Cherubims and pomegranates","Lions and oxen","Vines and clusters of grapes"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:5",verse:"And the greater house he cieled with fir tree, which he overlaid with fine gold, and set thereon palm trees and chains.", insight:"Palms spoke of life and chains of unity, wrought into the very walls. The house itself told stories to those who looked closely."},
{q:"With what was the house garnished?", options:["Precious stones","Ivory and ebony","Marble pillars","Painted plaster"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:6",verse:"And he garnished the house with precious stones for beauty: and the gold was gold of Parvaim.", insight:"Precious stones glittered on the walls, catching the lamplight. Beauty in God's house is not waste; it is worship made visible."},
{q:"From where did the gold for the temple come?", options:["Parvaim","Ophir","Sheba","Tarshish"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:6",verse:"And he garnished the house with precious stones for beauty: and the gold was gold of Parvaim.", insight:"The gold of Parvaim, famed for its purity, covered the house. When giving to God, Solomon chose the finest source he knew, not the nearest."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the most holy house?", options:["Twenty cubits long and twenty cubits broad","Ten cubits square","Sixty cubits long and twenty broad","Thirty cubits long and ten broad"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:8",verse:"And he made the most holy house, the length whereof was according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits: and he overlaid it with fine gold, amounting to six hundred talents.", insight:"The most holy place was a perfect cube, twenty cubits each way. Perfection of form whispered that the God within is perfect in every direction."},
{q:"How much fine gold overlaid the most holy house?", options:["Six hundred talents","Fifty shekels","One hundred talents","Three thousand talents"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:8",verse:"And he made the most holy house, the length whereof was according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits: and he overlaid it with fine gold, amounting to six hundred talents.", insight:"Six hundred talents of gold covered the innermost room. The costliest gift went to the holiest place, where only the high priest would see it. God sees what men never will."},
{q:"How much did the nails of gold weigh?", options:["Fifty shekels","Five hundred shekels","One talent","Six hundred shekels"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:9",verse:"And the weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. And he overlaid the upper chambers with gold.", insight:"Even the nails were weighed in gold, fifty shekels each. No detail is too small to be offered to God with excellence."},
{q:"What stood in the most holy house?", options:["Two cherubims of image work","The ark and the mercy seat only","Two golden candlesticks","The altar of incense"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:10",verse:"And in the most holy house he made two cherubims of image work, and overlaid them with gold.", insight:"Two cherubim stood guard over the holy place, as at Eden's gate. They remind us that God's holiness is beautiful, but it is never casual."},
{q:"How long was each wing of the cherubims?", options:["Five cubits","Ten cubits","Twenty cubits","Three cubits"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:11",verse:"And the wings of the cherubims were twenty cubits long: one wing of the one cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing was likewise five cubits, reaching to the wing of the other cherub.", insight:"Each wing stretched five cubits, so the pair spanned the room. Worship, like those wings, should stretch to cover all of life."},
{q:"What did the wings of the cherubims touch?", options:["The walls of the house, and each other in the midst","The ark and the vail","The floor and the ceiling","The doors of the oracle"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:12",verse:"And one wing of the other cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing was five cubits also, joining to the wing of the other cherub.", insight:"Wingtip to wingtip and wall to wall, the cherubim filled the space. There was no gap in their covering, a picture of God's complete protection."},
{q:"Which way did the faces of the cherubims look?", options:["Inward","Toward the doors","Upward to heaven","Downward to the ark"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:13",verse:"The wings of these cherubims spread themselves forth twenty cubits: and they stood on their feet, and their faces were inward.", insight:"The cherubim faced inward, toward each other and the ark. In God's presence, even angels turn their attention fully toward Him."},
{q:"Of what was the vail of the temple made?", options:["Blue, purple, and crimson, and fine linen, with cherubims wrought in","White linen only","Scarlet and goats' hair","Blue and purple, without figures"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:14",verse:"And he made the vail of blue, and purple, and crimson, and fine linen, and wrought cherubims thereon.", insight:"The veil's rich colors and woven cherubim marked the boundary of God's throne room. It taught Israel that access to God is precious, and one day it would be torn open for all."},
{q:"How high were the two pillars Solomon made before the house?", options:["Thirty-five cubits","Twenty cubits","Eighteen cubits","Twelve cubits"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:15",verse:"Also he made before the house two pillars of thirty and five cubits high, and the chapiter that was on the top of each of them was five cubits.", insight:"The twin pillars rose thirty-five cubits, visible from afar. God gives His people landmarks of faith that can be seen from a distance."},
{q:"How many pomegranates adorned the wreaths on the chapiters?", options:["A hundred","Four hundred","Seventy","Fifty"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:16",verse:"And he made chains, as in the oracle, and put them on the heads of the pillars; and made an hundred pomegranates, and put them on the chains.", insight:"A hundred golden pomegranates ringed each capital, fruitfulness carved in metal. God's house was decorated with the emblem of a fruitful life."},
{q:"What were the names of the two pillars?", options:["Jachin and Boaz","Hiram and Huram","Urim and Thummim","Gerizim and Ebal"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 3:17",verse:"And he reared up the pillars before the temple, one on the right hand, and the other on the left; and called the name of that on the right hand Jachin, and the name of that on the left Boaz.", insight:"Jachin means He shall establish, and Boaz means in Him is strength. The temple's very pillars preached, and every entrance to worship passed between those promises."}
]},
{n:4, name:"Furnishing the House", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 4:1",verse:"Moreover he made an altar of brass, twenty cubits the length thereof, and twenty cubits the breadth thereof, and ten cubits the height thereof."}, facts:["Did you know the bronze sea was a giant basin about fifteen feet across, standing on twelve bronze oxen and holding three thousand baths of water? It was the priests' place of washing.","Did you know Solomon multiplied the tabernacle's furnishings: ten lampstands instead of one, ten tables instead of one, and ten lavers for washing? The greater house called for greater provision.","Did you know the bronze vessels were cast in clay molds in the Jordan valley between Succoth and Zeredathah, and there was so much bronze that Solomon never even weighed it?"], questions:[
{q:"What were the dimensions of the altar of brass Solomon made?", options:["Twenty cubits long, twenty broad, and ten high","Ten cubits square and five high","Thirty cubits long and ten broad","Twenty cubits long and five high"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:1",verse:"Moreover he made an altar of brass, twenty cubits the length thereof, and twenty cubits the breadth thereof, and ten cubits the height thereof.", insight:"The great bronze altar dwarfed the tabernacle's, twenty by twenty and ten high. The bigger the house of God, the bigger the place of sacrifice at its door."},
{q:"How wide was the molten sea, from brim to brim?", options:["Ten cubits","Five cubits","Twenty cubits","Thirty cubits"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:2",verse:"Also he made a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round in compass, and five cubits the height thereof; and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.", insight:"The molten sea spanned ten cubits, a basin of cleansing for the priests. Before serving God, His servants must be washed; purity comes before ministry."},
{q:"How high was the sea, and what was its circumference?", options:["Five cubits high and thirty cubits round","Ten cubits high and twenty round","Three cubits high and ten round","Five cubits high and ten round"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:2",verse:"Also he made a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round in compass, and five cubits the height thereof; and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.", insight:"Five high and thirty around, a vessel of generous proportions. God's provision for cleansing is never cramped or stingy."},
{q:"How many oxen stood under the molten sea?", options:["Twelve","Ten","Four","Three"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:4",verse:"It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea was set above upon them, and all their hinder parts were inward.", insight:"Twelve oxen bore the sea, one for each tribe. The whole people of God together uphold the ministry of cleansing."},
{q:"In which directions did the twelve oxen face?", options:["Three toward the north, three toward the west, three toward the south, and three toward the east","All twelve toward the east","Six toward the north and six toward the south","All twelve inward toward the sea"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:4",verse:"It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea was set above upon them, and all their hinder parts were inward.", insight:"The oxen faced every point of the compass while their hinder parts held the basin. God's cleansing is offered in every direction, to all who will come."},
{q:"How much water did the molten sea hold?", options:["Three thousand baths","One thousand baths","Ten thousand baths","Five hundred baths"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:5",verse:"And the thickness of it was an handbreadth, and the brim of it like the work of the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies; and it received and held three thousand baths.", insight:"Three thousand baths of water stood ready for the priests' washing. God stocks His house with more than enough grace for all who serve."},
{q:"How many lavers did Solomon make, and how were they placed?", options:["Ten, five on the right hand and five on the left","Twelve, in two rows of six","Five, all on the right side","Ten, all before the porch"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:6",verse:"He made also ten lavers, and put five on the right hand, and five on the left, to wash in them: such things as they offered for the burnt offering they washed in them; but the sea was for the priests to wash in.", insight:"Ten lavers, five aside, kept the work of washing close at hand. God multiplies the means of cleansing because He knows how often we need it."},
{q:"What were the lavers used for?", options:["Washing the burnt offering, while the sea was for the priests to wash in","Holding the oil for the lamps","Mixing the incense for the altar","Storing the showbread"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:6",verse:"He made also ten lavers, and put five on the right hand, and five on the left, to wash in them: such things as they offered for the burnt offering they washed in them; but the sea was for the priests to wash in.", insight:"The lavers washed the sacrifices and the sea washed the priests. Both the offering and the offerer must be clean before God."},
{q:"How many candlesticks of gold did Solomon make?", options:["Ten","Seven","Twelve","One"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:7",verse:"And he made ten candlesticks of gold according to their form, and set them in the temple, five on the right hand, and five on the left.", insight:"Ten golden lampstands instead of one, each burning before the oracle. The light of God's presence was multiplied in the new house, as His light multiplies in every faithful heart."},
{q:"Where were the candlesticks placed?", options:["Five on the right hand and five on the left, before the oracle","All ten in the most holy place","Five in the porch and five in the court","Around the brasen altar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:7",verse:"And he made ten candlesticks of gold according to their form, and set them in the temple, five on the right hand, and five on the left.", insight:"They stood before the oracle, five aside, burning after the manner appointed. True light always positions itself before God's word, not beside it."},
{q:"How many tables did Solomon make for the temple?", options:["Ten","Twelve","Seven","Two"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:8",verse:"He made also ten tables, and placed them in the temple, five on the right side, and five on the left. And he made an hundred basons of gold.", insight:"Ten tables held the showbread, the bread of God's presence. God spreads His table generously; there is always room for His people."},
{q:"How many basons of gold did Solomon make?", options:["A hundred","Fifty","Ten","A thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:8",verse:"He made also ten tables, and placed them in the temple, five on the right side, and five on the left. And he made an hundred basons of gold.", insight:"A hundred golden basins for the service of the house. When God's people give themselves to His work, He provides vessels for every task."},
{q:"What courts did Solomon make?", options:["The court of the priests and the great court","The inner court and the outer court only","The court of the women and the court of Israel","The upper court and the lower court"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:9",verse:"Furthermore he made the court of the priests, and the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid the doors of them with brass.", insight:"A court for the priests and a great court for the people, each with its place. God honors both set-apart ministry and the gathered congregation."},
{q:"Where did Solomon set the molten sea?", options:["On the right side of the east end, toward the south","In the midst of the court","Before the porch on the north","Beside the brasen altar on the west"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:10",verse:"And he set the sea on the right side of the east end, over against the south.", insight:"The sea stood at the southeast, right where the priests would pass. God places cleansing where we cannot avoid it on our way to serve."},
{q:"What did Huram finish making for the house of God?", options:["The pots, the shovels, and the basons","The doors, the hinges, and the bolts","The cherubims, the vail, and the pillars","The trumpets, the harps, and the cymbals"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:11",verse:"And Huram made the pots, and the shovels, and the basons. And Huram finished the work that he was to make for king Solomon for the house of God;", insight:"Pots, shovels, and basins sound humble, but Huram's name is honored for them. In God's house, no honest work is lowly."},
{q:"How many pomegranates were on the networks covering the chapiters?", options:["Four hundred, in two rows on each wreath","One hundred on each pillar","Seventy in a single row","Twelve, for the tribes"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:13",verse:"And four hundred pomegranates on the two wreaths; two rows of pomegranates on each wreath, to cover the two pommels of the chapiters which were upon the pillars.", insight:"Four hundred pomegranates in twin rows crowned the pillars. God loves abundance in beauty; His decorations are never bare minimum."},
{q:"Of what metal were the vessels Huram made for King Solomon?", options:["Bright brass","Pure gold","Silver","Iron"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:16",verse:"The pots also, and the shovels, and the fleshhooks, and all their instruments, did Huram his father make to king Solomon for the house of the LORD of bright brass.", insight:"Bright, polished bronze for the outer service, gold within. God assigns each vessel its metal and its place, and every one shines when it serves where He put it."},
{q:"Where were the vessels cast?", options:["In the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredathah","In the furnaces of Tyre","In the valley of Hinnom near Jerusalem","On the plain of Megiddo"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:17",verse:"In the plain of Jordan did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredathah.", insight:"They were cast in clay molds in the Jordan plain, far from Jerusalem. God often prepares His vessels in hidden, lowly places before bringing them into His house."},
{q:"What golden vessels did Solomon make for the house of God?", options:["The golden altar and the tables of showbread","The ark and the mercy seat","The seven lamps of the tabernacle","The censers of Aaron"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:19",verse:"And Solomon made all the vessels that were for the house of God, the golden altar also, and the tables whereon the shewbread was set;", insight:"A golden altar for incense and tables for the bread of presence. Prayer and fellowship with God belong at the very center of worship."},
{q:"Which of these were made of pure gold?", options:["The snuffers, the basons, the spoons, and the censers","The pots, the shovels, and the basons","The pillars and their chapiters","The lavers and their bases"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 4:22",verse:"And the snuffers, and the basons, and the spoons, and the censers, of pure gold: and the entry of the house, the inner doors thereof for the most holy place, and the doors of the house of the temple, were of gold.", insight:"Even the snuffers and spoons were pure gold. In God's service, the smallest instrument deserves the finest material."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Glory Fills the Temple", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 5:14",verse:"So that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of God."}, facts:["Did you know that when the ark was brought into the temple, it contained nothing but the two stone tables Moses had placed there at Horeb? The manna and Aaron's rod were gone by then.","Did you know the dedication music was led by Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun, with their families arrayed in white linen, and one hundred twenty priests sounding trumpets?","Did you know the priests could not even stand to minister because the cloud of God's glory filled the temple? It remains one of the most vivid pictures of God's presence in all of Scripture."], questions:[
{q:"What did Solomon bring into the house of God when all the work was finished?", options:["The silver, the gold, and the vessels which David his father had dedicated","The tribute of the surrounding nations","The spoils taken from the Philistines","The gifts of the queen of Sheba"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:1",verse:"Thus all the work that Solomon made for the house of the LORD was finished: and Solomon brought in all the things that David his father had dedicated; and the silver, and the gold, and all the instruments, put he among the treasures of the house of God.", insight:"Solomon completed what David had only prepared, bringing his father's dedicated treasures into the house. One generation's devotion becomes the next generation's foundation."},
{q:"Whom did Solomon assemble at Jerusalem for the dedication?", options:["The elders of Israel, the heads of the tribes, and the chief of the fathers","The captains of the army and the mighty men","The kings of the surrounding nations","The priests only"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:2",verse:"Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which is Zion.", insight:"The whole nation was represented: elders, tribal heads, and fathers. God's great moments are family affairs; everyone has a place at the dedication."},
{q:"Why were they assembled at Jerusalem?", options:["To bring up the ark of the covenant out of the city of David","To anoint Solomon king a second time","To divide the land among the tribes","To crown the new high priest"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:2",verse:"Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which is Zion.", insight:"The ark was coming home to the house built for it. Every true dedication centers on bringing God's presence into the middle of His people."},
{q:"When did all the men of Israel assemble themselves unto the king?", options:["In the seventh month, at the feast","In the first month, at the passover","In the third month, at Pentecost","In the tenth month, at the new year"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:3",verse:"Wherefore all the men of Israel assembled themselves unto the king in the feast which was in the seventh month.", insight:"They gathered in the seventh month, at the feast of tabernacles. God's timing wove the dedication into the festival of His dwelling with His people."},
{q:"Who took up the ark?", options:["The Levites","The priests alone","The elders of Israel","Solomon's mighty men"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:4",verse:"And all the elders of Israel came; and the Levites took up the ark.", insight:"The Levites bore the ark as the law commanded. God's presence is carried by consecrated hands, not by convenience."},
{q:"What else did the priests and Levites bring up besides the ark?", options:["The tabernacle of the congregation and all the holy vessels","The throne of David and the crown","The tribute gold of Ophir","The stones of the old altar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:5",verse:"And they brought up the ark, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that were in the tabernacle, these did the priests and the Levites bring up.", insight:"The old tabernacle and its vessels were brought up too, honored, not discarded. God does not throw away the past when He builds the future."},
{q:"What did Solomon and all the congregation sacrifice before the ark?", options:["Sheep and oxen that could not be told nor numbered","A thousand burnt offerings, as at Gibeon","Seven bullocks and seven rams","Two goats for a sin offering"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:6",verse:"Also king Solomon, and all the congregation of Israel that were assembled unto him before the ark, sacrificed sheep and oxen, which could not be told nor numbered for multitude.", insight:"The sacrifices were beyond counting. When God's presence takes center stage, generosity overflows all measurement."},
{q:"Where did the priests set the ark?", options:["In the oracle of the house, under the wings of the cherubims","In the porch before the doors","In the court beside the altar","In the treasury with the dedicated things"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:7",verse:"And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD unto his place, to the oracle of the house, into the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubims:", insight:"The ark rested beneath the cherubim's wings in the most holy place. At last, God's throne had its room, and His people had their meeting place."},
{q:"What did the cherubims' wings do over the ark?", options:["They spread themselves forth over the ark and its staves, covering them","They folded down behind the ark","They touched the vail on either side","They lifted the ark from the floor"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:8",verse:"For the cherubims spread forth their wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubims covered the ark and the staves thereof above.", insight:"The cherubim spread their wings in sheltering covering over the ark. God's presence is both majestic and tender, guarded and welcoming."},
{q:"What could be seen of the staves of the ark?", options:["Their ends were seen from the ark before the oracle, but not without","They were removed and laid in the treasury","They reached from wall to wall of the house","They were overlaid with silver"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:9",verse:"And they drew out the staves of the ark, that the ends of the staves were seen from the ark before the oracle; but they were not seen without. And there it is unto this day.", insight:"The staves' ends peeked out, a reminder that the ark had journeyed. God lets us see hints of the road He has traveled with us."},
{q:"How long did the ark remain there?", options:["Unto this day","Until the captivity only","Seven years","Forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:9",verse:"And they drew out the staves of the ark, that the ends of the staves were seen from the ark before the oracle; but they were not seen without. And there it is unto this day.", insight:"Unto this day, says the chronicler. God's settled presence is not a visit; He comes to stay."},
{q:"What was inside the ark?", options:["Nothing save the two tables which Moses put therein at Horeb","The pot of manna and Aaron's rod only","The book of the law written by Moses","The stones from the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:10",verse:"There was nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moses put therein at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of Egypt.", insight:"Only the two tables of the covenant remained within. At the heart of God's house is His word, His covenant promises, kept safe."},
{q:"When had those tables been placed in the ark?", options:["At Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with Israel coming out of Egypt","At Sinai, before the golden calf","At Kadesh in the wilderness","At Gilgal after crossing Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:10",verse:"There was nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moses put therein at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of Egypt.", insight:"The tables dated to Horeb, to the covenant at the exodus. God's faithfulness has a long memory, and His promises do not expire."},
{q:"What was unusual about the priests on that day?", options:["All who were present were sanctified, and did not then wait by course","Only the high priest entered the holy place","They wore sackcloth instead of linen","They offered no sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:11",verse:"And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy place: (for all the priests that were present were sanctified, and did not then wait by course:", insight:"Every priest was sanctified and served, course divisions set aside. In moments of God's glory, all hands are consecrated and all are welcome to serve."},
{q:"Which three men led the Levitical singers, with their sons and brethren?", options:["Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun","Korah, Dathan, and Abiram","Ethan, Joel, and Abijah","Shemaiah, Uriel, and Asaiah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:12",verse:"Also the Levites which were the singers, all of them of Asaph, of Heman, of Jeduthun, with their sons and their brethren, being arrayed in white linen, having cymbals and psalteries and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them an hundred and twenty priests sounding with trumpets:)", insight:"Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun led the choirs David had appointed. Worship prepared in one generation resounds in the next."},
{q:"How many priests sounded with trumpets?", options:["A hundred and twenty","Seventy","Twelve","A thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:12",verse:"Also the Levites which were the singers, all of them of Asaph, of Heman, of Jeduthun, with their sons and their brethren, being arrayed in white linen, having cymbals and psalteries and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them an hundred and twenty priests sounding with trumpets:)", insight:"One hundred twenty trumpets joined the singers as one sound. When God's people praise together, heaven takes notice."},
{q:"What did the trumpeters and singers do as one?", options:["They lifted up their voice to praise and thank the LORD","They marched seven times around the temple","They read the law from morning till noon","They offered incense on the golden altar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:13",verse:"It came even to pass, as the trumpeters and singers were as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD; and when they lifted up their voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of musick, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever: that then the house was filled with a cloud, even the house of the LORD;", insight:"They were as one in praising God, trumpet and voice blended. Unity in worship is itself an offering God loves."},
{q:"What words did they sing?", options:["For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever","Holy, holy, holy is the LORD of hosts","Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised","The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:13",verse:"It came even to pass, as the trumpeters and singers were as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD; and when they lifted up their voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of musick, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever: that then the house was filled with a cloud, even the house of the LORD;", insight:"Their song was simple: God's goodness and everlasting mercy. The deepest worship often says the simplest true thing."},
{q:"Why could the priests not stand to minister?", options:["Because of the cloud, for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of God","Because the trumpets were too loud","Because the sacrifices were too many","Because the king commanded them to kneel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:14",verse:"So that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of God.", insight:"The cloud of God's glory stopped the service in its tracks. When God Himself shows up, even the best-planned worship gives way to wonder."},
{q:"What is said of the priests present when the cloud filled the house of God?", options:["All the priests that were present were sanctified","Only the high priest was present","They had fled in fear","They were still sacrificing outside"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 5:11",verse:"And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy place: (for all the priests that were present were sanctified, and did not then wait by course:", insight:"Every priest present was sanctified. God fills houses where His servants have prepared their hearts."}
]}
]);
